title: A Political Truce with Staal?
subtitle: We must either confirm or deny a supposed deal between the Greater Worker's Guild and the chancellor.
view-if: chancellor = "Staal" and staal_time and staal_time < 6 and staal_marcher_r >= 3 and staal_marcher_support >= 6 and not staal_plan
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/schleicher_work.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= Political Truce with Staal

With Tobias Leighart’s announcement that he would support a Staal cabinet if Goodryke were the only alternative, numerous leaks have surfaced to the public—much to the annoyance of those in the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. Many workers still view Staal as merely a continuation of the despised Goodryke cabinet, and it remains in our electoral interest to uphold total opposition to him.

Meanwhile, the Greater Worker's Guild has sought to shape Staal’s proposed public works program, and has come round to his argument that the state needs a stretch of calm to recover—that a parliamentary ousting now would only pave the way for Goodryke’s return, or for something worse standing behind him. The specifics of our negotiations have been exaggerated—and in many cases, outright misreported—creating a serious public relations crisis among the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>’s working-class base.

What should our stance be moving forward?

- @yay
- @nay

@yay
title: Let the Free Guilds talk.
unavailable-subtitle: The party is too distrustful of Staal to allow this.
choose-if: staal_marcher_support >= 6 and labor_strength >= (center_strength*2) + left_strength
on-arrival: staal_marcher_support += 2; staal_marcher_r += 1 if staal_marcher_r < 5; commons_marcher -= 4; disfavored_marcher -= 4; center_dissent += 10; knight_dissent += 10; staal_marcher_adopted = 1; staal_approval += 1

In a public statement, the Greater Worker's Guild stops short of denying rumors of a political truce, instead arguing that the chancellor should be given a few months free from parliamentary interference to implement his public works program. The move has been justified to the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> leadership by claiming it would peel voters away from both the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, while benefiting the workers we represent.

Needless to say, the Free Guild representing the very workers who suffered under his predecessor has lost credibility in their eyes.

@nay
title: Pure disinformation, we never discussed a 'political truce'.
on-arrival: staal_marcher_r -= 1; labor_dissent += 5

Such nonsense, we will deny the fake news and distance ourself from the chancellor to prevent more incidents.